kit: sdlc
version: 0.1.0
source: bamr87/bamr87 templates/sdlc/
seeded-by: |
  Copied per repo (not inherited). Run by hand or by an adoption PR until
  tools/fanout.sh learns `--kit sdlc` (Fleet Ops). Substitute the fan-out
  tokens, pick ONE release/release-please-config.<type>.json by repo type and
  copy it to the root as release-please-config.json, and fill the TODO: lines
  in AGENTS.md. Never overwrite an existing CHANGELOG.md, AGENTS.md or ADR log.
files: sdlc.yml, sdlc.schema.json, AGENTS.template.md, CLAUDE.template.md, CHANGELOG.template.md, docs/README.template.md, docs/adr/README.md, docs/adr/0000-template.md, docs/adr/0001-record-architecture-decisions.md, release/release.yml, release/release-please-config.simple.json, release/release-please-config.node.json, release/release-please-config.python.json, release/release-please-config.ruby.json, release/.release-please-manifest.json, content-queue/backlog.yml
targets: sdlc.yml -> .github/sdlc.yml; AGENTS.template.md -> AGENTS.md; CLAUDE.template.md -> CLAUDE.md; CHANGELOG.template.md -> CHANGELOG.md; docs/README.template.md -> docs/README.md; docs/adr/* -> docs/adr/; release/release.yml -> .github/workflows/release.yml; release/release-please-config.<type>.json -> release-please-config.json; release/.release-please-manifest.json -> .release-please-manifest.json; content-queue/backlog.yml -> _data/backlog.yml (module content_queue only); sdlc.schema.json stays in the hub
spec: specs/WORK.md UPS-WORK-01/04/05/12, specs/AGENT-CONTEXT.md UPS-AGENT-07/08/09, specs/REPOSITORY.md UPS-REPO-21, specs/QUALITY.md UPS-QA-32/33; checker contract specs/WORK.contract.yml
tests: templates/sdlc/test_sdlc_kit.py (stdlib + PyYAML; jsonschema used when installed)
updated: 2026-10-03
changelog: |
  0.1.0 — initial kit (SDLC harmonization Wave 1). The core per-repo SDLC
  files. `.github/sdlc.yml` (schema sdlc/v1, validated by sdlc.schema.json)
  declares type (decision D6), backlog mode (D1: Issues by default), modules,
  adr_path (D2) and release type (D5). AGENTS.md is the canonical agent file
  and CLAUDE.md a pointer that imports it with @AGENTS.md (D4). Every repo,
  content repos included, gets a release-please CHANGELOG through the hub's
  reusable release-please.yml at @v1 (D5), with one config per release type:
  simple for docs/content, sites, demos and the control plane; node, python,
  ruby for packaged apps and libraries.
notes: |
  - Placeholders are the fan-out tokens only: __PROJECT_NAME__,
    __DEFAULT_BRANCH__, __KIT_VERSION__. Hand-filled spots are `TODO:` lines,
    which UPS-AGENT-07 requires to be gone before a repo passes.
  - ruby config: version-file defaults to lib/__PROJECT_NAME__/version.rb; fix
    the path when the gem name differs from the repo name.
  - CHANGELOG.template.md seeds a `## [0.1.0] - baseline` heading so
    release-please inserts new entries under the intro instead of re-writing the
    `# Changelog` title. Match it to the manifest version on adoption.
  - The spec-driven module's tools are their own kit, templates/spec-driven/.
  - Snapshot a file into archive/ BEFORE changing it (same rule as every kit).
